WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:04.940
Just as Pennywise from Stephen King's IT has
many faces, the terrifying monster clown is

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:07.660
too big an idea for just one franchise.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:11.010
Creepy clowns have appeared in a wide variety
of movies over the years, and they're just

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.600
as terrifying now as they ever were.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:16.500
Here are some movies featuring deadly clowns
you might not have met—and who may haunt

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:18.390
your nightmares once you do.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.040
"See you in your dreams."

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.040
Clown

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:25.462
Brought to you by future Spider-Man: Homecoming
director Jon Watts, Clown was shot in 2012,

00:00:25.462 --> 00:00:30.250
but it took until 2016 to find distribution
in the U.S.

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:34.250
It's a genuinely disturbing film, featuring
one of the most terrifyingly inhuman clowns

00:00:34.250 --> 00:00:36.350
ever to appear onscreen.

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:40.140
Kent's just a regular guy, but when his son's
birthday party is almost ruined after the

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.870
clown cancels, Kent puts on an old suit and
plays the role himself.

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:47.970
Unfortunately, the suit is cursed, and he
starts transforming into a demonic clown with

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.540
an insatiable need to eat the flesh of children.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.870
So… have fun with that.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:53.960
Stitches

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:58.260
Stitches wasn't a very good clown to begin
with, but his career—and his life—ended

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.530
when some kids tied his shoelaces together
and he fell onto an upturned knife and died.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:06.649
Six years later, those kids are teenagers
having a party in the same house, and Stitches

00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:11.500
rises again to take his revenge, complete
with Go Go Gadget clown murder arms.

00:01:16.460 --> 00:01:18.139
All Hallows' Eve

00:01:18.139 --> 00:01:22.109
In the three part anthology All Hallows' Eve,
a babysitter working on Halloween finds a

00:01:22.109 --> 00:01:25.200
videotape of a murdering clown in a kid's
Trick or Treat bag.

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.369
Soon, the clown on the tape begins to appear
in the real world.

00:01:28.369 --> 00:01:33.479
All Hallows' Eve director Damien Leone created
Art the Clown years before the movie's 2013

00:01:33.479 --> 00:01:38.090
release for his short films Terrifier and
The 9th Circle, both of which were incorporated

00:01:38.090 --> 00:01:39.689
into All Hallow's Eve.

00:01:39.689 --> 00:01:44.599
The killer clown is set to return in Leone's
next film, a feature-length version of Terrifier.

00:01:44.599 --> 00:01:45.599
Amusement

00:01:45.599 --> 00:01:50.619
This 2008 film is split into sections focusing
on three girls attempting to escape from a

00:01:50.619 --> 00:01:52.729
maniac in clown makeup.

00:01:52.729 --> 00:01:56.950
Before he became the masked clown, this movie's
main character was a psychologically unbalanced

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.840
child who was picked on by those same three
girls.

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:04.239
Now that they're all grown, he's hunting them
down and taking revenge.

00:02:04.239 --> 00:02:05.239
Clownhouse

00:02:05.239 --> 00:02:10.420
It's basically the perfect setup for a low-budget
1989 horror movie: three escaped mental patients

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:14.860
kill some clowns at the circus and steal their
costumes, then follow three teenage brothers

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:17.030
home to their big, isolated house.

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:18.660
Creepy music and murder ensue.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.080
Unfortunately, the real-life circumstances
of Clownhouse's production turned out to be

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:31.450
far more disturbing than its story.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:35.110
Director Victor Salva was convicted of molesting
the actor who played the youngest brother,

00:02:35.110 --> 00:02:39.630
and the story resurfaced when Salva, after
a brief prison stay, was hired by Disney to

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.850
direct Powder in 1995.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:46.460
Anyone who knows the story is understandably
going to find Clownhouse hard to watch.

00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:48.270
Blood Harvest

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:52.990
Mervo the Marvelous is unique among the clowns
on this list—he's not necessarily the killer

00:02:52.990 --> 00:02:56.680
in Blood Harvest, he's just hanging around,
being creepy, in the town where the killings

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:57.850
are happening.

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:02.430
Played by Tiny Tim, the falsetto-singing ukulele
player, Mervo is the older brother of the

00:03:02.430 --> 00:03:04.680
ex-boyfriend of Jill, the film's protagonist.

00:03:04.680 --> 00:03:08.010
"I brought you some flowers, Jill."

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:12.350
When everyone who Jill cares about starts
dying, Mervo is one of the possible suspects,

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:16.460
obviously - when people are mysteriously dropping
dead, that guy in town who likes to wear clown

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.580
makeup is going to look pretty suspicious.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:22.340
Blood Harvest turned out to be little more
than a footnote in Tiny Tim's unusual career,

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:25.850
but it's certainly weird enough to be worth
a look for enthusiasts of the clown horror

00:03:25.850 --> 00:03:27.240
subgenre.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.240
Vulgar

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:31.560
Have you ever wanted to watch Jay and Silent
Bob fight a killer clown?

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.460
Well, Vulgar's your chance.

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:38.010
Kevin Smith produced and acted in this ultra
low budget 2000 horror comedy about a murderous

00:03:38.010 --> 00:03:41.570
clown named Vulgar who wants revenge on the
men who assaulted him.

00:03:41.570 --> 00:03:45.390
Vulgar was directed by Bryan Johnson, and
stars Brian O'Halloran, best known as Dante

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:47.780
from Clerks, in the title role.

00:03:47.780 --> 00:03:49.600
Killer Klowns from Outer Space

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:54.430
After its 1988 release, Killer Klowns from
Outer Space became a minor cult classic, but

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:57.290
it's not as widely remembered or beloved as
it once was.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:01.319
It tells the story of clownlike aliens who
arrive on Earth in flying saucers that look

00:04:01.319 --> 00:04:05.510
like circus tents and begin massacring and
eating all the humans they find, often in

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:08.300
ridiculous ways that resemble circus performances.

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:18.020
Killer Klowns from Outer Space was the only
film written and directed by the Chiodo Brothers,

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:22.749
special effects artists who also created the
titular monsters for the Critters movies.

00:04:22.749 --> 00:04:23.860
Gacy

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:27.650
John Wayne Gacy might be the scariest killer
clown of all, for the simple reason that he

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.050
actually existed.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:33.020
A family man and respected community member,
Gacy turned out to have the bodies of more

00:04:33.020 --> 00:04:35.699
than 30 people buried underneath his house.

00:04:35.699 --> 00:04:41.169
The bio-pic Gacy came out in 2003, and while
it's not a widely remembered or popular film,

00:04:41.169 --> 00:04:44.159
it's a must-see if you're interested in true
crime or killer clowns.

00:04:44.159 --> 00:04:46.599
"Now we aren't strangers, are we?"

00:04:46.599 --> 00:04:47.599
Thanks for watching!

00:04:47.599 --> 00:04:49.650
